; regression test for a real retrofit gap: `invimplies` (backwards implication, alias `⇐`)
; had full syntax declared in propositional.kurt (`infix`, `prop`, `chain`, `alias`) but, unlike every
; other operator there, had no defining axiom relating it to `implies` at all -- a
; pre-existing gap that didn't matter before selective export (everything was unconditionally
; exported regardless of axioms) but became a real, observable break after: nothing exported
; ever mentioned `invimplies`, so its syntax silently stopped surviving `load propositional`. Fixed by
; adding the natural definitional axiom relating it to `implies`. Confirmed here: `invimplies`
; parses as infix, `⇐` resolves as its alias, and the defining axiom lets a genuine
; `invimplies`-based derivation go through.
load propositional
prop A, B
use A implies B
B ⇐ A
